description:
Change under review: let customers download invoice PDFs straight from object storage instead of streaming them through the API. For the changed file, only the changed region is shown; the rest of the file is unchanged and compiles.

`src/routes/invoices.ts` (changed, lines 30-41):
```ts
30 app.get("/invoices/:id/download", requireSession, async (req) => {
31   const invoice = await invoices.findById(req.params.id);
32   if (invoice === undefined || invoice.customerId !== req.session.customerId) {
33     return new Response("not found", { status: 404 });
34   }
35   const url = await getSignedUrl(
36     s3,
37     new GetObjectCommand({ Bucket: INVOICE_BUCKET, Key: invoice.pdfKey }),
38     { expiresIn: 60 },
39   );
40   return Response.redirect(url, 302);
41 });
```

`getSignedUrl` and `GetObjectCommand` come from the AWS SDK v3. The returned URL carries a SigV4 signature, and a session token from the service's temporary role credentials, in its query string; together they allow reading that one object for 60 seconds. `INVOICE_BUCKET` is private, and `invoice.pdfKey` is set by the server when it generates the invoice. `requireSession` sets `req.session.customerId` from the signed session cookie. Request logging records the method, route pattern and status code, not query strings or response headers.
